This requires honesty about a major doctrine before you invest time drafting federal filings.

The Younger Abstention Barrier. Under Younger v. Harris, 401 U.S. 37 (1971), federal courts do not interfere with pending state criminal proceedings, even when constitutional violations are alleged. The policy is that state courts must be given the opportunity to resolve constitutional claims first. For your pending criminal cases, Younger is the threshold problem for any federal injunctive or declaratory relief.

